#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ft-voiced: Frametop Voice, local dictation and wake words (frametop-voice.service).

One PipeWire capture stream (pw-record) feeds two consumers:
  * dictation: push-to-talk -> record -> Moonshine (live, on the CPU) or whisper-server -> the
    input relay types the text where typing goes
  * wake word: sherpa-onnx keyword spotter -> capture the spoken command -> whisper-server ->
    a voice command (voice_commands.py), or the command hook and event subscribers

Push-to-talk comes from the input relay (a key combination or mouse button with the dictate or
dictate_hold action: "toggle|start|stop|cancel <source>" on @frametop_voice, taken only from this
user) and from Frame controller buttons, read from SteamVR's web socket (input/vrws.py), so they
still do what they do in games. Text goes to the relay as "type TEXT" on @frametop_relay; it
types only while no modifier is held, so letters never turn into shortcuts.

Runs in Frametop's container (scripts/in-box: numpy, sherpa-onnx and pw-record are there),
named ft-voiced for pkill. Programs it starts for voice commands and hooks run on the host
(distrobox-host-exec), as the relay's commands do. Settings: voice_settings.py. Models:
~/.local/share/frametop/voice/models (voice/models.sh). Control socket for ft-voice:
/run/user/UID/frametop-voice/control.sock.
"""
